      "content": "The first and historically most important application for communication satellites was in intercontinental long distance telephony. The fixed Public Switched Telephone Network relays telephone calls from land line telephones to an earth station, where they are then transmitted to a geostationary satellite. The downlink follows an analogous path. Improvements in submarine communications cables through the use of fiber-optics caused some decline in the use of satellites for fixed telephony in the late 20th century.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.0,
      "temperature": 0.0,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
      "persistent": true,
